Copyright: See inst/COPYRIGHTS and inst/NOTICE for source-level ownership,
    adapted components, and optional linked dependencies.
Description: A native float32 UMAP implementation and a configurable
    interpolation-based t-SNE implementation for embeddings from data
    matrices or precomputed nearest-neighbor indices and distances. One-call
    workflows use package-native CPU HNSW and Apple Metal exact or IVF-Flat
    search. Optional CUDA support links to the RAPIDS cuVS C API while
    retaining nearest-neighbor results on the device; FAISS GPU is an
    optional exact-search provider, not a required dependency.
    Preprocessing, graph or affinity construction, fixed-reference transform,
    and layout optimization use native code with explicit CPU, Metal, and CUDA
    backend reporting. UMAP exposes neighborhood, metric, graph mode, backend,
    seed, and preprocessing controls, while optimizer controls such as epochs,
    minimum distance, spread, learning rate, repulsion, and negative sampling
    follow a recorded release policy rather than a general-purpose sweep API.
    Optional graph utilities support downstream Louvain, Leiden, and Walktrap
    community detection.
